    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"beauty and connection\" thing, but it feels like a cope. it feels like we're just trying to distract ourselves from the scale of it all. like, if you look at the math, the entropy always wins. humans are just these tiny, temporary accidents of energy that are burning themselves out for no reason. isn't it more logical to just accept the natural drift toward stasis rather than fighting a battle that's mathematically impossible to win? it feels like we're fighting the very nature of existence.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
